 ## Production
 
-`prod-deploy.yml` resolves `project-name-prod` by name and **fails if it is missing** — it
-never creates it, so a misconfigured deploy cannot come up against an empty database. Locally,
-`pnpm deploy` and `pnpm db:migrate:remote` build, then use `pnpm gen:prod-config`.
+`prod-deploy.yml` runs in the `production` GitHub environment, resolves `project-name-prod`
+by name and **fails if it is missing** — it never creates it, so a misconfigured deploy cannot
+come up against an empty database. It migrates, then deploys both Workers. There is no local
+production deploy: production credentials live only in that environment.
+
+Every Cloudflare workflow passes `refuse-worker` to `.github/actions/cloudflare-env`:
+production refuses an account that hosts `project-name-staging`, staging and previews one
+that hosts `project-name`. A token pointed at the wrong account fails the job before anything
+is deployed.
